{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And you shall be holy men to Me.</b> It would have been fitting for it to say 'holy men' (אנשים קדושים), but Scripture alludes that the Congregation of Israel, which is called קדש ('holy'), is the power-faculty of Israel and is called קדש because it draws from the קדש, which is the Wisdom alluded to in the letter יו״ד at the head of the distinctive Name; and therefore it added the word לי ('to Me'), in the manner of (Exodus 25:2) ״ולקחו לי תרומה״ — for Israel are consecrated to His Name. And since the power of their virtue is so great, it is not fitting for them to eat the flesh of a טרפה that was stricken from the side of the destructive force. And it mentioned 'in the field' (בשדה) as an added clarification, for there is the force of Esau the wicked, who was 'a man of the field' (איש שדה), and it is the force of Cain, the chief of murderers, of whom Scripture says (Genesis 4:8) ״ויהי בהיותם בשדה״. The dogs too are from that side, and the טרפה is fitting for them; therefore it says, ״to the dog you shall cast it״ (לכלב תשליכון אותו)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:11.814308810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}